OpenStreetMap Geo API
This repository contains a containerized Python API designed to query and interact with geographic data from OpenStreetMap. The project leverages a modern web framework and is built to be easily deployed using Docker.

Key Features
Containerized with Docker: The entire application is packaged within a Docker container, ensuring a consistent and reproducible environment.

RESTful API Interface: Exposes geographic data through a clean and easy-to-use API, making it simple to integrate into other applications.

OpenStreetMap Integration: Uses OpenStreetMap data as its source for geocoding, routing, or other geo-related queries.

Scalable Architecture: Designed with a modular structure that allows for easy expansion and the addition of new features.

Technologies Used
Python 3

A Python web framework (e.g., Flask, FastAPI)

Docker

OpenStreetMap data services

Getting Started
Prerequisites
Before you begin, ensure you have Docker installed on your system.

Installation and Running the API
Clone this repository to your local machine:

Bash

git clone https://github.com/MaxMoya/opengeo-openstreetmap.git
cd opengeo-openstreetmap
Build the Docker image:

Bash

docker build -t opengeo-api .
Run the container. This will start the API and map the container's port (e.g., 8000) to a local port.

Bash

docker run -d -p 8000:8000 --name opengeo-container opengeo-api
-d: Runs the container in detached mode (in the background).

-p 8000:8000: Maps port 8000 on your local machine to port 8000 inside the container.

--name opengeo-container: Gives the container a memorable name.

The API should now be running and accessible at http://localhost:8000.

API Endpoints
The API provides several endpoints for interacting with geographic data. Here is a plausible example of the kind of endpoints you can expect:

Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/v1/geocode	Geocodes an address or place name to coordinates.
GET	/api/v1/reverse-geocode	Reverse geocodes coordinates to a street address.
GET	/api/v1/search	Searches for points of interest (e.g., parks, restaurants) within a specified area.

Export to Sheets
Example: Geocoding a location

You can make a GET request to the geocode endpoint with a location parameter.

Request:

GET http://localhost:8000/api/v1/geocode?location=Eiffel%20Tower,%20Paris
Example Response:

JSON

{
  "location": "Eiffel Tower, Paris",
  "latitude": 48.8584,
  "longitude": 2.2945,
  "address": "Champ de Mars, 5 Avenue Anatole France, 75007 Paris, France"
}
Project Structure
app.py: The main entry point for the web application, responsible for initializing the API.

opengeo_api.py: Contains the core logic for handling geocoding and other geographic data processing.

Dockerfile: Specifies the environment and instructions for building the Docker image.

Potential Use Cases
Building a custom geocoding or search service.

Integrating geographic data into web or mobile applications.

Data analysis on OpenStreetMap datasets.

Developing a routing or mapping application.
